      "answer": {
        "lead": "Not as a full two days of PTO: Thursday 2026-11-12 and Friday 2026-11-13 need 2 days, and you have 1.5 available.",
        "policy_facts": [
          {
            "text": "I assumed \"next Thursday and Friday\" means 2026-11-12 and 2026-11-13. That is 2 PTO days, with no company holidays on those dates.",
            "citations": [],
            "data_sources": [
              {
                "tool": "check_policy_compliance"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "text": "Your available PTO is 1.5 days (12.5 accrued, 10.0 used, 1.0 pending), which is less than the 2 days requested.",
            "citations": [],
            "data_sources": [
              {
                "tool": "check_pto_balance"
              },
              {
                "tool": "check_policy_compliance"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "text": "Your PTO balance can't go negative, and Ridgeline doesn't advance PTO from future pay periods. If a request is longer than your balance, you can reduce it or request unpaid personal leave for the remainder.",
            "citations": [
              {
                "doc_id": "RSE-PTO-01",
                "section": "3.3",
                "snippet": "Your PTO balance cannot go negative. You can only take PTO you have already accrued."
              },
              {
                "doc_id": "RSE-PTO-01",
                "section": "3.3",
                "snippet": "unpaid personal leave is approved by HR"
              }
            ],
            "data_sources": []
          },
          {
            "text": "Notice isn't a problem. Requests of 3 PTO days or fewer have no minimum notice. If the balance were enough, your manager, Ben Carter, would approve a 2-day request.",
            "citations": [
              {
                "doc_id": "RSE-PTO-01",
                "section": "4.2",
                "snippet": "Requests of 3 PTO days or fewer have no minimum notice: submit them as early as practical."
              }
            ],
            "data_sources": [
              {
                "tool": "check_policy_compliance"
              }
            ]
          }
        ],
        "recommendations": [
          {
            "text": "Take one of the two days as PTO, for example Thursday 2026-11-12. That fits within your 1.5 available days."
          },
          {
            "text": "Ask HR about unpaid personal leave for the other day. Talk to your manager, Ben Carter, and HR early about it."
          },
          {
            "text": "I can draft a message to Ben Carter about a shortened PTO request, or open an HR ticket about unpaid leave for the remaining day. Tell me which you'd like."
          }
        ]
